            <div class="zn-element zn-lg  ">
              <div id="" class="zn-text "   ><p>If you’re in the middle of binge-watching “The White Lotus,” you best finish before sojourning to Treetop Hideaways in east Tennessee. </p><p><br></p><p>“We intentionally do not have televisions in the treehouses, and encourage our guests to enjoy nature and connect,” said Joy Taylor, general manager.</p><p><br></p><p>But what these arboreal accommodations lack in high-definition drama, they make up for in woodsy whimsy (think reclaimed barnwood, penny-tiled bathrooms, and vintage-style gramophone speakers). There’s also air conditioning for those muggy Tennessee nights and Wi-Fi for sending a quick email or two.  </p><p><br></p><p>Of course, you won’t want to waste too much time staring at a screen. After all, Ruby Falls — an underground waterfall tucked deep within Lookout Mountain — is just a short drive away. There’s also the River Gallery Sculpture Garden in downtown Chattanooga, where you can gander at world-class art before retiring to the trees.</p></div>
